$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2,6-Dibenzylpyridines 3a-i and 2,6-Dibenzyl-4-methylpyridines 4a—i;
General Procedure To a magnetically stirred mixture of
2,6-dibromopyridine (17; 150 mg, 0.63 mmol) or
2,6-dibromo-4-methylpyridine (18; 157 mg, 0.63 mmol) and Pd[PPh3]4 (8
mol%) in anhyd THF (6 mL) was added the corresponding benzylzinc reagent
in THF (7 mL of 0.5 M solution, 3.6 equiv) over 5 min. The reaction
mixture was stirred and heated at 50 °C for 24 h. After cooling, the
reaction was quenched with sat. aq NH4Cl (3 mL) and the solvent was
evaporated under reduced pressure. The residue was taken up with H2O (25
ml), extracted with CH2Cl2 (2 x 15 mL), and the combined extracts were
dried (MgSO4). After concentration, the brown residue was purified by
column chromatography using cyclohexane-EtOAc (10:1 → 5:1) or
hexane-CHCl3 (4:1 → 1:1) solvent systems. The synthesis of 3a and 4a was
repeated using catalytic system based on Pd(OAc)2 (6%) and S-Phos (10%).
Under this condition full conversion of substrates was observed in less
then 3 h. 2,6-Dibenzylpyridine (3a) Yield: 136 mg (83%); colorless oil 1H
NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 4.16 (s, 4 H, 2 x CH2), 6.87 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 2
H, H-3py and H-5py), 7.16-7.30 (m, 10 H, Hph), 7.43 (t, J = 7.7 Hz, 1 H,
H-4py). 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 44.9, 120.7, 126.5, 128.7, 129.4,
137.1, 139.8, 160.7. MS (EI, 70 eV): m/z (%) = 258 (100), 259 (46), 180
(19), 167 (11), 166 (10),91 (7), 153 (4), 115 (4). HRMS: m/z [M + Na]+
calcd for C19H17N + Na: 282.1259; found: 282.1260.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM catalyst Pd(OAc)2-S-Phos gave full conversion after 3h, Negishi
cross-coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Suzuki-Miyaura and Negishi approaches to a series of forensically
relevant pyridines and pyrimidines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Blachut, Dariusz; Szawkalo, Joanna; Czarnocki, Zbigniew
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2011), (21), 3496-3506

