$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the multicomponent
domino Heck-Negishi reaction: To an oven-dried ground test tube equipped
with a magnetic stir bar, 9-benzyl-6-chloropurine 1a (0.1 mmol, 24.4 mg),
Pd(PPh3)4 (11.5 mg, 10 mol %) and t-butyl acrylate 2a (0.3 mmol, 44 µL)
were added. The test tube sealed with threaded rubber stopper was
evacuated and backfilled with N2 (this process was repeated for 3 times),
and then THF (1.0 mL) was added via syringe. The solution was stirred for
5 min at room temperature and then benzylzinc bromide (3a) (4.0 equiv,
0.5 mL of 0.805 M solution in THF) was added slowly via syringe. The
mixture was stirred at 70 °C until 1a was disappeared (monitored by TLC).
The reaction mixture was quenched with saturated NH4Cl solution (2.0 mL)
and extracted with ethyl acetate (10.0 mL). The organic phase were dried
over Na2SO4, and concentrated under vacuum. The resulted residue was
purified by flash chromatography over silica gel (ethyl acetate/petroleum
ether). The desired product 4a as buff oil (77% yield). The structure of
4a was confirmed by 1H NMR, 13C NMR, HRMS, HMQC, HMBC and COSY. Entry: 5
Product: 5a; Yield: 83%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Highly Regioselective Three-Component Domino Heck-Negishi Coupling
Reaction for the Functionalization of Purines at C6
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wang, Dong-Chao; Niu, Hong-Ying; Xie, Ming-Sheng; Qu, Gui-Rong; Wang,
Hui-Xuan; Guo, Hai-Ming
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(1), 262-265

