aryl iodides and secondary alkylzinc iodides: 3-(sec-Butyl)phenol (Table
2, Row 2, Column 2, Entry 2). The general procedure was employed with the
following modifications: 2.5 equiv. alkylzinc reagent employed, 5 mol%
NiCl2 and terpyridine employed, reaction conducted at 80 ºC, 14 h
reaction time. A colorless liquid (120 mg, 80%) was isolated by column
chromatography (gradient from 70:30 to 65:35 Hex:EtOAc). 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δ: 7.16 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 6.77 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 1H), 6.66 (m,
2H), 4.86 (s, 1H), 2.55 (app. sextet, J = 7.3 Hz, 1H), 1.58 (m, 2H), 1.22
(d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H), 0.83 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 3H) ppm. 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3) δ: 155.5, 150.0, 129.5, 119.9, 114.1, 112.8, 41.7, 31.2, 21.9,
12.4 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective (>100:1 s-Bu product:n-Bu product), Negishi cross-coupling
reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nickel-Catalyzed Negishi Cross-Coupling Reactions of Secondary Alkylzinc
Halides and Aryl Iodides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
