$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure 2 (TP2): Cross-coupling
reactions of adamantylzinc reagents. The desired aryl halide (0.9 equiv)
was added to the freshly prepared zinc reagent followed by Pd(OAc)2 (1
mol%) and SPhos (2 mol%) and the mixture was stirred for the given time
at 50 °C. The reaction mixture was quenched with sat. NH4Cl solution (10
mL) and extracted with EtOAc (3×20 mL). The combined organic phases were
dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated in vacuo. The crude residue obtained
was purified by flash column chromatography to give the analytically pure
product. Preparation of 2,7-di(adamantan-1-yl)-fluorene (4i). The
cross-coupling reaction of 2a (3.2 mL, 1.0 mmol, 0.32 M in THF) with
Pd(OAc)2 (2 mg, 0.01 mmol), SPhos (8 mg, 0.02 mmol) and
2,7-dibromo-fluorene (3k, 146 mg, 0.45 mmol) was performed according to
TP2 in 3 h. Flash column chromatography (silica, pentane:Et2O 9:1)
furnished 4i as a white solid. Yield: 82%. m.p.: 308.9-311.8 °C. 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm) = 7.70 (d, J=8.3Hz, 2H), 7.57 (s, 2H), 7.39 (d,
J=8.0Hz, 2H), 3.88 (s, 2H), 2.16 (bs, 6H), 2.02 (brs, 12H), 1.73-1.91 (m,
12H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm) = 149.8, 143.3, 139.3, 123.3,
121.4, 119.1, 43.5, 37.2, 36.9, 36.4, 29.1. MS (70 eV, EI), m/z (%) = 434
(M+, 100), 313 (3), 135 (33), 107 (3), 93 (7), 79 (6), 67 (3). HRMS (EI),
m/z calc. for C33H38 (434.2974): 434.2961. IR (ATR) υ (cm-1) = 2898,
2846, 1649, 1604, 1474, 1446, 1414, 1344, 1314, 1262, 1247, 1176, 1100,
1079, 1068, 1060, 1038, 976, 875, 861, 827, 800, 742, 714, 694, 673.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Negishi reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Substituted Adamantylzinc Reagents Using a Mg-Insertion in
the Presence of ZnCl2 and Further Functionalizations
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Saemann, Christoph; Dhayalan, Vasudevan; Schreiner, Peter R.; Knochel,
Paul
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(9), 2418-2421

