$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the cross-coupling of
aryl iodides and secondary alkylzinc iodides: 3-(iso-Propyl)phenol (Table
2, Row 2, Column 2, Entry 1). The general procedure was employed with the
following modifications: 2.5 equiv. alkylzinc reagent employed, 5 mol%
NiCl2 and terpyridine employed, reaction conducted at 80 ºC, 17 h
reaction time. A colorless liquid (110 mg, 81%) was isolated by column
chromatography (gradient from 70:30 to 65:35 Hex:EtOAc). 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δ: 7.16 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 6.81 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 6.71 (m,
1H), 6.67 (m, 1H), 4.70 (bs, 1H), 2.86 (septet, J = 6.8 Hz, 1H), 1.24 (d,
6.8 Hz, 6H) ppm. 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 155.6, 151.1, 129.6, 119.2,
113.5, 112.7, 34.1, 24.0 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective (>100:1 i-Pr product:n-Pr product), Negishi cross-coupling
reaction
