$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the cross-coupling of
aryl iodides and secondary alkylzinc iodides: Ethyl
3-(3,5-dimethylphenyl)butanoate (Table 3, Row 1, Column 2). The general
procedure was employed with the following modifications: 5 mol% NiCl2 and
terpyridine employed, 15 h reaction time, reaction conducted at 80 ºC. 1H
NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 6.84 (app. s, 3H), 4.10 (q, J = 7.3 Hz, 2H), 3.21
(m, 1H), 2.50–2.60 (m, 2H), 2.30 (s, 6H), 1.28 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H), 1.21
(t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H) ppm. 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 172.6, 145.9, 138.0,
128.1, 124.7, 60.3, 43.2, 36.5, 21.9, 21.5, 14.3 ppm. IR (neat, cm-1):
2967, 2920, 2872, 1736, 1606, 1462, 1286, 1176, 1159, 1030, 847, 704.
Anal. Calcd. for C14H20O2: C, 76.33; H, 9.15. Found: C, 76.53; H, 9.26.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Negishi cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nickel-Catalyzed Negishi Cross-Coupling Reactions of Secondary Alkylzinc
Halides and Aryl Iodides
