$DATUM Typical procedure for cross-coupling reactions of zinc reagents 1f and
aryl bromide (TP5) To a solution of aryl bromide (0.5 mmol) in THF (0.5
mL) were added S-Phos (12 mg, 6 mol%), Pd(OAc)2 (3.4 mg, 3 mol%). Then, a
solution of benzyl zinc chloride 1f (0.75 mmol, 1.5 eq.) in THF-DMSO was
added dropwise (Eq. (3)). The reaction mixture was stirred for 10-24 h at
25 °C, then quenched by adding sat. aqueous NH4Cl. The layers were
separated and the aqueous layer was extracted with diethyl ether (5 × 50
mL). The combined organic extracts were dried over Na2SO4. Evaporation of
the solvents in vacuo and purification by flash chromatography (silica
gel, isohexane/EA = 10:1). The title coupling products (3a'-3g). Ethyl
4-(2-(2-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)-2-methylpropanamido)-1-phenylpropyl)benzoate
(3a', according to TP5). A yellowish oil, d.r. > 5:95 (anti/syn).
anti-isomer: 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 7.95 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 7.23
(d, J = 7.6 Hz, 2H),7.33-7.21 (m, 5H), 6.75 (br, 1H), 4.83-4.79 (m,1H),
4.33 (q, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 3.84 (d, J = 10.8 Hz, 1H), 1.35 (t, J = 7.2 Hz,
3H), 1.34 (s, 3H), 1.10 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 3H), 0.79 (s, 9H), 0.05 (s, 3H),
-0.07 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 175.5, 166.5, 147.8, 141.6,
130.1, 129.0, 128.5, 128.1, 128.0, 126.9, 76.5, 61.0, 59.1, 47.1, 27.7,
27.5, 25.9, 20.5, 18.7, 14.2, -2.4. IR (KBr, cm-1) ν 3375, 1720, 1647,
1574, 1227,1180, 1030. MS (EI, 70 eV): m/z (%) = 468 [M+-Me] (4), 426
(11), 244(25), 173 (100), 115 (12), 73 (42). HRMS (EI): calcd for
C28H41NO4Si: 483.2805, found: 483.2801.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Negishi coupling, >95:5 anti:syn
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Stereoselective C(sp3)-C(sp2) Negishi coupling of
(2-amido-1-phenylpropyl)zinc compounds through the steric control of
β-amido group
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
