$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Negishi Cross-Coupling Reaction; General
Procedure 2 Halide (10 mmol), Pd2dba3·CHCl3 (263 mg, 0.25 mmol, 2.5
mol%), dppf (282 mg, 0.5 mmol, 5 mol%), THF (75 mL) and the organozinc
reagent solution 1 (14 mmol, 1.4 equiv) were stirred for 24-48 h at 50 °C
under argon atmosphere. The reaction mixture was allowed to cool to 25
°C, quenched with sat. NH4Cl (20 mL) and extracted several times with
EtOAc. The combined organic phases were washed with H2O (10 mL) and brine
(10 mL) and dried (Na2SO4). After removal of all volatiles, the residue
was purified by column chromatography (Table 2). Ethyl
3-(2-Methoxynaphthalen-1-yl)propiolate (2) Prepared from
1-iodo-2-methoxynaphthalene (5.67 g, 19.6 mmol) and 1 (94 mL, 23.5 mmol),
following General Procedure 2; The spectroscopic data are in accordance
with the published data.16 Ethyl 3-Naphthalen-1-ylpropiolate (26) This
compound was obtained after the reaction between 1-iodonaphthalene (15;
1.7 g, 6.7 mmol) and 1 (30.2 mL, 9.4 mmol), following General Procedure
2. 77% yield (1.16 g). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 8.34 (d, J = 8.4 Hz,
1 H), 7.93 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1 H), 7.85 (ddd, J = 7.3, 4.8, 1.2 Hz, 1 H),
7.62 (ddd, J = 8.4, 6.8, 1.5 Hz, 1 H), 7.54 (ddd, J = 8.3, 6.8, 1.4 Hz, 1
H), 7.45 (dd, J = 7.3, 1.1 Hz, 1 H), 4.36 (q, J = 7.1 Hz, 2 H), 1.40 (t,
J = 7.1 Hz, 3 H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 154.3, 133.8, 133.2,
133.0, 131.4, 128.5, 127.7, 127.0, 125.8, 125.2, 117.3, 85.5, 85.4, 62.3,
14.3. MS (GC-MS): m/z (%) = 224 (57, [M+]), 179 (65), 152 (100), 139
(10). HRMS (EI): m/z calcd for C15H12O2 (M+): 224.0832; found: 224.0828.
